/-!
# A set of generators for the quasi-coherent modules on a flat groupoid in algebraic spaces

Let `(U, R, s, t, c)` be a groupoid in algebraic spaces with `s` and `t` flat.  Stacks 0780 asserts
that there is a *set* `T` of quasi-coherent modules on the groupoid such that every
quasi-coherent module on it is the directed colimit of those of its submodules which are
isomorphic to a member of `T`.  This file proves it, with `T` a type of the universe of the
schemes.

## The proof

Choose a presentation `U = W/R₀` of the space of objects by a scheme `W` (Stacks 0263), with atlas
`φ : W ⟶ U`.  Put `Q = R ×_{t, U, φ} W` and `R_W = Q ×_{s, U, φ} W`, the space of arrows of `R`
together with a lift of their target and of their source to `W`, with the two lifts
`t_W, s_W : R_W ⟶ W` and the map `ψ : R_W ⟶ R`.  The map `s_W` is flat, a base change of `s`
after an étale map, and `ψ` is étale and surjective, so `ψ^*` is faithful.

For a quasi-coherent module `(ℱ, α)` on the groupoid, `φ^*ℱ` is a quasi-coherent module on the
scheme `W`, and `α` read along `ψ` is a morphism `α_W : t_W^*φ^*ℱ ⟶ s_W^*φ^*ℱ`.  The closure step of
Stacks 077U (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_eq`) puts every local
section of `φ^*ℱ` into a submodule `ℰ_W ⊆ φ^*ℱ` generated by at most `κ` sections over each affine
open and invariant under `α_W`, with `κ` depending only on the groupoid and the chosen charts.

The space `R₀ = W ×_U W` maps to `R_W` by `(w₁, w₂) ↦ (e(φ w₁), w₁, w₂)`, and along that map `α_W`
becomes, by the unit condition of `(ℱ, α)`, the canonical descent datum of `φ^*ℱ`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartTransition_reindex_eq_unflatten`).  So `ℰ_W` is a submodule of
`φ^*ℱ` with its descent datum, and by Stacks 03M3 it descends to a quasi-coherent submodule
`ℰ ⊆ ℱ` with `φ^*ℰ ≅ ℰ_W`.  Invariance of `ℰ` under `α` holds after `ψ^*`, which is faithful and
a left adjoint, hence holds, and `(ℰ, α|ℰ)` is a submodule of `(ℱ, α)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_bounded_submodule_of_chart_section`).

The modules `ℰ` so obtained have a set of isomorphism classes: `ℰ_W` is `κ`-generated
(Stacks 077M), over a fixed underlying module the transition morphisms form a set, and `ℰ` is
determined by `ℰ_W` with its descent datum.  A set of representatives is therefore a separating
family of `QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)`, which is then a Grothendieck abelian category, and in a
Grothendieck abelian category the quotients of finite sums of copies of a separator are a set as
required (`CategoryTheory.IsGrothendieckAbelian.exists_family_isFiltered_isColimit`).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartTransition_reindex_eq_unflatten`: the transition morphism read on
  the chart, restricted to `W ×_U W`, is the canonical descent datum.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_bounded_submodule_of_chart_section`: every
  local section on the chart lies in a bounded submodule.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_isSeparating`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.hasSeparator` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.isGrothendieckAbelian`: `QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)` has a
  separating family indexed by a small type, hence a separator, and is a Grothendieck abelian
  category, for `s` and `t` flat.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_small_generating_family` is
  **Stacks 0780**.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0780](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0780)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 077U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 077Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 077M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03M3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03M3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe w u

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-- Pullbacks of presheaves on the big fppf site over `S` (instance search times out without
this shortcut). -/
local instance (priority := high) hasPullback_presheaf_quasicoherentGeneratingSet
    {X Y Z : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (f : X ⟶ Z) (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    HasLimit (cospan f g) :=
  HasLimitsOfShape.has_limit _

/-! ### A transition morphism read on a chart -/

section Transport

variable {T X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-- Two canonical identifications of inverse images compose to the one along the composite
equality. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem pullbackTransport_trans (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) {f g k : T ⟶ X}
    (h₁ : f = g) (h₂ : g = k) :
    pullbackTransport F h₁ ≫ pullbackTransport F h₂ = pullbackTransport F (h₁.trans h₂) := by
  subst h₁ h₂
  simp [pullbackTransport]

/-- The canonical identification along an equality of a morphism with itself is the
identity. -/
theorem pullbackTransport_self (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) {f : T ⟶ X} (h : f = f) :
    pullbackTransport F h = 𝟙 _ := by
  simp [pullbackTransport]

/-- The reindexing of a morphism between two inverse images, written out. -/
theorem modulePullbackReindex_eq {Y Z : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f : T ⟶ Y) {a b : Y ⟶ Z}
    {M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Z.1 Z.2}
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS a).obj M ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS b).obj M) :
    modulePullbackReindex f α = (modulePullbackCompIso B S hS f a).inv.app M ≫
      (modulePullback B S hS f).map α ≫ (modulePullbackCompIso B S hS f b).hom.app M := by
  rw [modulePullbackReindex]

/-- **Flattening a morphism between two inverse images of an inverse image is natural in the
module.** -/
theorem modulePullbackFlatten_naturality {Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (g : Y ⟶ X)
    {a b : T ⟶ Y} {M N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (ζ : (modulePullback B S hS a).obj ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M) ⟶
      (modulePullback B S hS b).obj ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M))
    (ξ : (modulePullback B S hS a).obj ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj N) ⟶
      (modulePullback B S hS b).obj ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj N))
    (hζ : ζ ≫ (modulePullback B S hS b).map ((modulePullback B S hS g).map f) =
      (modulePullback B S hS a).map ((modulePullback B S hS g).map f) ≫ ξ) :
    modulePullbackFlatten g ζ ≫ (modulePullback B S hS (b ≫ g)).map f =
      (modulePullback B S hS (a ≫ g)).map f ≫ modulePullbackFlatten g ξ := by
  simp only [modulePullbackFlatten]
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.EquivariantQuasicoherentPullback.comp_naturality₃_comp_left
    ((modulePullbackCompIso B S hS a g).inv.naturality f).symm hζ
    ((modulePullbackCompIso B S hS b g).hom.naturality f).symm

end Transport

/-- **Compatibility of two transition morphisms along a morphism of modules**: for `a, b : V ⟶ W`,
a morphism `ι : ℰ ⟶ 𝒩` and `β : a^*ℰ ⟶ b^*ℰ`, `γ : a^*𝒩 ⟶ b^*𝒩`, the square
`β ≫ b^*ι = a^*ι ≫ γ`. -/
def IsTransitionSquare {V W : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (a b : V ⟶ W)
    {N EW : Modules.{u, u} B S hS W.1 W.2} (ι : EW ⟶ N)
    (β : (modulePullback B S hS a).obj EW ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS b).obj EW)
    (γ : (modulePullback B S hS a).obj N ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS b).obj N) : Prop :=
  β ≫ (modulePullback B S hS b).map ι = (modulePullback B S hS a).map ι ≫ γ

section Calculus

variable {U R W Rw : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {t s : R ⟶ U} {φ : W ⟶ U} {tw sw : Rw ⟶ W}
  {ψ : Rw ⟶ R} (ha : tw ≫ φ = ψ ≫ t) (hb : ψ ≫ s = sw ≫ φ)

/-- A transition morphism `α : t^*ℱ ⟶ s^*ℱ`, read along a morphism `ψ : R_W ⟶ R` whose composites
with `t` and `s` lift along `φ : W ⟶ U` to `t_W, s_W : R_W ⟶ W`, as a morphism
`t_W^*φ^*ℱ ⟶ s_W^*φ^*ℱ`.

The body is written at `CategoryTheory.comp₃`, for the reason given at
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.transitionPair`: a consumer must be able to see through the definition
without the kernel unfolding the transports. -/
def chartTransition (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F) :
    (modulePullback B S hS tw).obj ((modulePullback B S hS φ).obj F) ⟶
      (modulePullback B S hS sw).obj ((modulePullback B S hS φ).obj F) :=
  modulePullbackUnflatten φ
    (comp₃ (pullbackTransport F ha) (modulePullbackReindex ψ α) (pullbackTransport F hb))

/-- Flattened, the transition morphism read on a chart is the reindexing of `α` along `ψ`, as a
row composite. -/
theorem modulePullbackFlatten_chartTransition₃ (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F) :
    modulePullbackFlatten φ (chartTransition ha hb F α) =
      comp₃ (pullbackTransport F ha) (modulePullbackReindex ψ α) (pullbackTransport F hb) :=
  modulePullbackFlatten_unflatten φ _

/-- Flattened, the transition morphism read on a chart is the reindexing of `α` along `ψ`. -/
theorem modulePullbackFlatten_chartTransition (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F) :
    modulePullbackFlatten φ (chartTransition ha hb F α) =
      pullbackTransport F ha ≫ modulePullbackReindex ψ α ≫ pullbackTransport F hb :=
  (modulePullbackFlatten_chartTransition₃ ha hb F α).trans (comp₃_eq _ _ _)

/-- `ψ^*α` read through the comparisons `ψ^* t^* ≅ (ψ ≫ t)^*` and `ψ^* s^* ≅ (ψ ≫ s)^*` of
Stacks 03LU is the reindexing of `α` along `ψ`. -/
theorem comparisonTransition_compIso {V : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f : V ⟶ R)
    (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F) :
    comparisonTransition (modulePullbackCompIso B S hS f t) (modulePullbackCompIso B S hS f s) α =
      modulePullbackReindex f α := by
  rw [comparisonTransition, modulePullbackReindex_eq]

/-- **A transition morphism compatible on the chart is compatible on `R`.**  If
`β' : (t_W ≫ φ)^*ℰ ⟶ (s_W ≫ φ)^*ℰ` is compatible along `ι : ℰ ⟶ ℱ` with the reindexing of `α`
along `ψ`, `ψ^*` is faithful and `s^*ι` is a monomorphism, then `t^*ι ≫ α` factors through
`s^*ι`. -/
theorem exists_comp_eq_of_chart [(modulePullback B S hS ψ).Faithful]
    {E F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2} (ι : E ⟶ F) [Mono ((modulePullback B S hS s).map ι)]
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F)
    (β' : (modulePullback B S hS (tw ≫ φ)).obj E ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS (sw ≫ φ)).obj E)
    (hβ' : β' ≫ (modulePullback B S hS (sw ≫ φ)).map ι =
      (modulePullback B S hS (tw ≫ φ)).map ι ≫
        (pullbackTransport F ha ≫ modulePullbackReindex ψ α ≫ pullbackTransport F hb)) :
    ∃ β : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj E ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj E,
      β ≫ (modulePullback B S hS s).map ι = (modulePullback B S hS t).map ι ≫ α := by
  refine exists_comp_eq_of_comparison (modulePullback B S hS t) (modulePullback B S hS s)
    (modulePullback B S hS ψ) (modulePullback B S hS (ψ ≫ t)) (modulePullback B S hS (ψ ≫ s))
    (modulePullbackCompIso B S hS ψ t) (modulePullbackCompIso B S hS ψ s) ι α
    (pullbackTransport E ha.symm ≫ β' ≫ pullbackTransport E hb.symm) ?_
  rw [comparisonTransition_compIso]
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [← pullbackTransport_naturality ι hb.symm, reassoc_of% hβ']
  simp only [pullbackTransport_trans, pullbackTransport_self, Category.comp_id]
  rw [← pullbackTransport_naturality_assoc ι ha.symm]
  simp only [pullbackTransport_trans_assoc, pullbackTransport_self, Category.id_comp]

variable {R₀ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {t₀ s₀ : R₀ ⟶ W} (k : R₀ ⟶ Rw) (hkt : k ≫ tw = t₀)
  (hks : k ≫ sw = s₀) (hφ : t₀ ≫ φ = s₀ ≫ φ) {e : U ⟶ R} {x : R₀ ⟶ U} {n : R₀ ⟶ R}
  (hn : k ≫ ψ = n) (hxe : x ≫ e = n)

include hxe in
/-- The reindexing of `α` along a morphism `n` factoring through the unit `e` is a transport, by
the unit condition `e^*α = 1`. -/
theorem modulePullbackReindex_eq_transport_of_unit (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F)
    (het : e ≫ t = e ≫ s) (hu : modulePullbackReindex e α = pullbackTransport F het)
    (hns : n ≫ t = n ≫ s) :
    modulePullbackReindex n α = pullbackTransport F hns := by
  have e₁ : x ≫ e ≫ t = n ≫ t := by rw [← Category.assoc, hxe]
  have e₂ : n ≫ s = x ≫ e ≫ s := by rw [← Category.assoc, hxe]
  have e₃ : x ≫ e ≫ t = x ≫ e ≫ s := by rw [het]
  have h2 := modulePullbackReindex_comp' (modulePullbackCompIsoAssoc B S hS) x e n hxe α e₁ e₂
  rw [hu, modulePullbackReindex_pullbackTransport x het F e₃] at h2
  have h3 : modulePullbackReindex n α =
      pullbackTransport F e₁.symm ≫ pullbackTransport F e₃ ≫ pullbackTransport F e₂.symm := by
    rw [h2]
    simp only [Category.assoc, pullbackTransport_trans, pullbackTransport_trans_assoc,
      pullbackTransport_self, Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id]
  rw [h3, pullbackTransport_trans, pullbackTransport_trans]

include hkt hks hφ hn hxe in
/-- **The transition morphism read on a chart, restricted along a lift of the unit, is the
canonical descent datum.**  If `k : R₀ ⟶ R_W` lifts `t₀, s₀ : R₀ ⟶ W` (with `t₀ ≫ φ = s₀ ≫ φ`) and
`k ≫ ψ` factors through the unit `e`, then by the unit condition `e^*α = 1` the reindexing of
the transition morphism along `k` is the transport of `ℱ` along `t₀ ≫ φ = s₀ ≫ φ`.

The computation is carried out with the named flattening
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullbackFlatten'`, which keeps every composite along `φ` out of
the objects of the module categories; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Groupoids/EquivariantQuasicoherentPullback.lean`. -/
theorem chartTransition_reindex_eq_unflatten (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F)
    (het : e ≫ t = e ≫ s) (hu : modulePullbackReindex e α = pullbackTransport F het) :
    pullbackTransport ((modulePullback B S hS φ).obj F) hkt.symm ≫
        modulePullbackReindex k (chartTransition ha hb F α) ≫
        pullbackTransport ((modulePullback B S hS φ).obj F) hks =
      modulePullbackUnflatten φ (pullbackTransport F hφ) := by
  have h₁ : (k ≫ tw) ≫ φ = n ≫ t := by rw [Category.assoc, ha, ← Category.assoc, hn]
  have h₂ : (k ≫ sw) ≫ φ = n ≫ s := by rw [Category.assoc, ← hb, ← Category.assoc, hn]
  have hns : n ≫ t = n ≫ s := h₁.symm.trans ((congrArg (· ≫ φ) hkt).trans
    (hφ.trans ((congrArg (· ≫ φ) hks).symm.trans h₂)))
  apply modulePullbackFlatten'_injective φ (rfl : t₀ ≫ φ = t₀ ≫ φ) (rfl : s₀ ≫ φ = s₀ ≫ φ)
  rw [modulePullbackFlatten'_comp_morphism φ rfl h₁ rfl,
    modulePullbackFlatten'_comp_morphism φ h₁ h₂ rfl,
    modulePullbackFlatten'_pullbackTransport φ rfl h₁ hkt.symm F
      ((congrArg (· ≫ φ) hkt.symm).trans h₁),
    modulePullbackFlatten'_reindex_of_flatten (modulePullbackCompIsoAssoc B S hS) φ ψ F α
      (chartTransition ha hb F α) (modulePullbackFlatten_chartTransition ha hb F α) k n hn h₁ h₂,
    modulePullbackFlatten'_pullbackTransport φ h₂ rfl hks F
      (h₂.symm.trans (congrArg (· ≫ φ) hks)),
    modulePullbackReindex_eq_transport_of_unit hxe F α het hu hns,
    modulePullbackFlatten'_eq_comp, modulePullbackFlatten_unflatten]
  simp only [pullbackTransport_trans]

include hkt hks hφ hn hxe in
/-- **A submodule invariant under the transition morphism read on a chart is invariant under the
canonical descent datum.** -/
theorem exists_descentTransition_of_chartTransition (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F)
    (het : e ≫ t = e ≫ s) (hu : modulePullbackReindex e α = pullbackTransport F het)
    {EW : Modules.{u, u} B S hS W.1 W.2} (ιW : EW ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS φ).obj F)
    (βW : (modulePullback B S hS tw).obj EW ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS sw).obj EW)
    (hβW : βW ≫ (modulePullback B S hS sw).map ιW =
      (modulePullback B S hS tw).map ιW ≫ chartTransition ha hb F α) :
    ∃ β₀ : (modulePullback B S hS t₀).obj EW ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s₀).obj EW,
      β₀ ≫ (modulePullback B S hS s₀).map ιW =
        (modulePullback B S hS t₀).map ιW ≫ modulePullbackUnflatten φ (pullbackTransport F hφ) := by
  refine ⟨pullbackTransport EW hkt.symm ≫ modulePullbackReindex k βW ≫ pullbackTransport EW hks,
    ?_⟩
  rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, ← pullbackTransport_naturality ιW hks,
    ← reassoc_of% (modulePullbackReindex_naturality k ιW hβW),
    ← pullbackTransport_naturality_assoc ιW hkt.symm,
    chartTransition_reindex_eq_unflatten ha hb k hkt hks hφ hn hxe F α het hu]



include hkt hks hφ hn hxe in
/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_descentTransition_of_chartTransition`, with the module `φ^*ℱ`,
the transition morphism read on the chart and the descent datum given through equations, so that
it applies whatever their spelling. -/
theorem exists_descentTransition_of_chartTransition' (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.1 U.2)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj F ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj F)
    (het : e ≫ t = e ≫ s) (hu : modulePullbackReindex e α = pullbackTransport F het)
    {N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS W.1 W.2} (hN : N = (modulePullback B S hS φ).obj F)
    {αW : (modulePullback B S hS tw).obj N ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS sw).obj N}
    (hαW : HEq αW (chartTransition ha hb F α))
    {αD : (modulePullback B S hS t₀).obj N ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s₀).obj N}
    (hαD : HEq αD (modulePullbackUnflatten φ (pullbackTransport F hφ)))
    {EW : Modules.{u, u} B S hS W.1 W.2} (ιW : EW ⟶ N)
    (βW : (modulePullback B S hS tw).obj EW ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS sw).obj EW)
    (hβW : IsTransitionSquare tw sw ιW βW αW) :
    ∃ β₀ : (modulePullback B S hS t₀).obj EW ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s₀).obj EW,
      IsTransitionSquare t₀ s₀ ιW β₀ αD := by
  subst hN
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hαW
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hαD
  exact exists_descentTransition_of_chartTransition ha hb k hkt hks hφ hn hxe F α het hu ιW βW hβW

end Calculus

/-! ### The chart of a groupoid in algebraic spaces -/

section Chart

variable {A : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (G : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces B S hS A)

/-- The chosen presentation of the space of objects of a groupoid in algebraic spaces. -/
abbrev objectsPresentation : Presentation B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property :=
  presentationOfIsAlgebraicSpace B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property

/-- The groupoid `W ×_U W ⇉ W` of the chosen presentation of the space of objects. -/
abbrev objectsGroupoid := presentationGroupoid (objectsPresentation G)

/-- The atlas `φ : W ⟶ U` of the space of objects. -/
abbrev objectsAtlas : (objectsGroupoid G).objects ⟶ G.objects :=
  presentationAtlas (objectsPresentation G)

/-- The space `R ×_{t, U, φ} W` of arrows with a lift of their target. -/
abbrev chartTargetFiber : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS :=
  AlgebraicSpaces.fiberProduct B S hS G.target (objectsAtlas G)

/-- The projection `R ×_{t, U, φ} W ⟶ R`. -/
abbrev chartTargetFiberArrow : chartTargetFiber G ⟶ G.arrows :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (pullback.fst G.target.hom (objectsAtlas G).hom)

/-- The projection `R ×_{t, U, φ} W ⟶ W`. -/
abbrev chartTargetFiberObject : chartTargetFiber G ⟶ (objectsGroupoid G).objects :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (pullback.snd G.target.hom (objectsAtlas G).hom)

/-- The space `R_W` of arrows with a lift of their target and of their source. -/
abbrev chartArrows : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS :=
  AlgebraicSpaces.fiberProduct B S hS (chartTargetFiberArrow G ≫ G.source) (objectsAtlas G)

/-- The projection `R_W ⟶ R ×_{t, U, φ} W`. -/
abbrev chartArrowsFst : chartArrows G ⟶ chartTargetFiber G :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (pullback.fst (chartTargetFiberArrow G ≫ G.source).hom (objectsAtlas G).hom)

/-- The lift `s_W : R_W ⟶ W` of the source. -/
abbrev chartSource : chartArrows G ⟶ (objectsGroupoid G).objects :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (pullback.snd (chartTargetFiberArrow G ≫ G.source).hom (objectsAtlas G).hom)

/-- The lift `t_W : R_W ⟶ W` of the target. -/
abbrev chartTarget : chartArrows G ⟶ (objectsGroupoid G).objects :=
  chartArrowsFst G ≫ chartTargetFiberObject G

/-- The map `ψ : R_W ⟶ R`. -/
abbrev chartArrowsMap : chartArrows G ⟶ G.arrows :=
  chartArrowsFst G ≫ chartTargetFiberArrow G

theorem isPullback_chartTargetFiber :
    IsPullback (chartTargetFiberArrow G) (chartTargetFiberObject G) G.target (objectsAtlas G) :=
  AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_fiberProduct B S hS G.target (objectsAtlas G)

theorem isPullback_chartArrows :
    IsPullback (chartArrowsFst G) (chartSource G) (chartTargetFiberArrow G ≫ G.source)
      (objectsAtlas G) :=
  AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_fiberProduct B S hS _ (objectsAtlas G)

/-- The lift of the target lies over the target. -/
theorem chartTarget_comp_objectsAtlas :
    chartTarget G ≫ objectsAtlas G = chartArrowsMap G ≫ G.target := by
  simp only [chartTarget, chartArrowsMap, Category.assoc]
  rw [(isPullback_chartTargetFiber G).w]

/-- The lift of the source lies over the source. -/
theorem chartArrowsMap_comp_source :
    chartArrowsMap G ≫ G.source = chartSource G ≫ objectsAtlas G := by
  simp only [chartArrowsMap, Category.assoc]
  exact (isPullback_chartArrows G).w

theorem objectsAtlas_isEtale : IsEtale B S hS (objectsAtlas G).hom :=
  presentationAtlas_isEtale _

theorem objectsAtlas_surjective :
    Function.Surjective (pointsMap B S hS _ (objectsAtlas G).hom) :=
  surjective_pointsMap_of_presheaf_surjective B S hS (objectsPresentation G).toSpace
    (objectsPresentation G).surjective

/-- The inverse image along the atlas of the space of objects is faithful. -/
theorem faithful_modulePullback_objectsAtlas :
    (modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).Faithful :=
  ⟨fun {_ _} χ χ' h => QuasiCoherentDescent.modulePullback_map_injective_of_isEtaleCovering B S hS
    (fun _ : Unit => (objectsGroupoid G).objects) (fun _ => objectsAtlas G)
    (presentationAtlas_isEtaleCovering _) χ χ' fun _ => h⟩

theorem chartTargetFiberArrow_isEtale : IsEtale B S hS (chartTargetFiberArrow G).hom :=
  isEtale_of_isPullback B S hS _ _ _ _ (isPullback_chartTargetFiber G).flip
    (objectsAtlas_isEtale G)

theorem chartArrowsFst_isEtale : IsEtale B S hS (chartArrowsFst G).hom :=
  isEtale_of_isPullback B S hS _ _ _ _ (isPullback_chartArrows G).flip (objectsAtlas_isEtale G)

/-- The map `ψ : R_W ⟶ R` is étale. -/
theorem chartArrowsMap_isEtale : IsEtale B S hS (chartArrowsMap G).hom :=
  isEtale_comp B S hS (chartArrowsFst_isEtale G) (chartTargetFiberArrow_isEtale G)

/-- The map `ψ : R_W ⟶ R` is surjective on points. -/
theorem chartArrowsMap_surjective :
    Function.Surjective (pointsMap B S hS _ (chartArrowsMap G).hom) := by
  have h1 := surjective_pointsMap_of_isPullback B S hS
    (AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_hom B S hS (isPullback_chartTargetFiber G).flip)
    (objectsAtlas_surjective G)
  have h2 := surjective_pointsMap_of_isPullback B S hS
    (AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_hom B S hS (isPullback_chartArrows G).flip)
    (objectsAtlas_surjective G)
  intro z
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := h1 z
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := h2 y
  exact ⟨w, pointsMap_comp_apply B S hS _ _ w⟩

/-- The inverse image along `ψ : R_W ⟶ R` is faithful, `ψ` being étale and surjective. -/
theorem faithful_modulePullback_chartArrowsMap :
    (modulePullback B S hS (chartArrowsMap G)).Faithful :=
  ⟨fun {_ _} χ χ' h => QuasiCoherentDescent.modulePullback_map_injective_of_isEtaleCovering B S hS
    (fun _ : Unit => chartArrows G) (fun _ => chartArrowsMap G)
    ⟨G.arrows.property, fun _ => (chartArrows G).property, fun _ => chartArrowsMap_isEtale G,
      by rw [Set.iUnion_const, Set.range_eq_univ]; exact chartArrowsMap_surjective G⟩
    χ χ' fun _ => h⟩

/-- The lift `s_W : R_W ⟶ W` of the source is flat when the source is. -/
theorem chartSource_isFlat (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom) :
    IsFlat B S hS (chartSource G).hom := by
  have h1 : IsFlat B S hS (chartTargetFiberArrow G).hom :=
    (isFlat_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback (isPullback_chartTargetFiber G).flip
      (isFlat_of_isEtale B S hS (objectsAtlas_isEtale G))
  have h2 : IsFlat B S hS (chartTargetFiberArrow G ≫ G.source).hom :=
    isFlat_comp B S hS (chartTargetFiber G).property G.arrows.property G.objects.property _ _ h1 hs
  exact (isFlat_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback (isPullback_chartArrows G) h2

/-- The arrow `(w₁, w₂) ↦ (e(φ w₁), w₁, w₂)` from `W ×_U W` to `R_W`. -/
def chartUnitArrow : (objectsGroupoid G).arrows ⟶ chartArrows G :=
  (isPullback_chartArrows G).lift
    ((isPullback_chartTargetFiber G).lift
      ((objectsGroupoid G).target ≫ objectsAtlas G ≫ GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow G)
      (objectsGroupoid G).target (by
        simp only [Category.assoc, GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow_comp_target,
          Category.comp_id]))
    (objectsGroupoid G).source (by
      rw [← Category.assoc, IsPullback.lift_fst]
      simp only [Category.assoc, GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow_comp_source,
        Category.comp_id]
      exact presentationAtlas_comm _)

theorem chartUnitArrow_chartTarget :
    chartUnitArrow G ≫ chartTarget G = (objectsGroupoid G).target := by
  simp only [chartUnitArrow, chartTarget]
  rw [← Category.assoc, IsPullback.lift_fst, IsPullback.lift_snd]

theorem chartUnitArrow_chartSource :
    chartUnitArrow G ≫ chartSource G = (objectsGroupoid G).source := by
  simp only [chartUnitArrow]
  rw [IsPullback.lift_snd]

theorem chartUnitArrow_chartArrowsMap :
    chartUnitArrow G ≫ chartArrowsMap G =
      (objectsGroupoid G).target ≫ objectsAtlas G ≫ GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow G := by
  simp only [chartUnitArrow, chartArrowsMap]
  rw [← Category.assoc, IsPullback.lift_fst, IsPullback.lift_fst]

/-- The two projections of `W ×_U W` have the same composite with the atlas. -/
theorem objectsAtlas_comm :
    (objectsGroupoid G).target ≫ objectsAtlas G = (objectsGroupoid G).source ≫ objectsAtlas G :=
  presentationAtlas_comm _

/-- The functor `ℱ ↦ (φ^*ℱ, can)` from quasi-coherent modules on the space of objects to the
groupoid of its chosen presentation. -/
def objectsFunctor :
    QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property ⥤
      QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G) :=
  quasicoherentFromSpaceBase B S hS (objectsGroupoid G) (objectsAtlas G) (presentationAtlas_comm _)

/-- **Stacks 03M3** for the chosen presentation of the space of objects: the functor
`ℱ ↦ (φ^*ℱ, can)` is an equivalence. -/
instance isEquivalence_objectsFunctor : (objectsFunctor G).IsEquivalence :=
  isEquivalence_quasicoherentFromSpaceBase B S hS (objectsGroupoid G) (objectsAtlas G)
    (presentationAtlas_isEtale _) (presentationAtlas_comm _) (presentationAtlas_isEtaleCovering _)
    (presentationAtlas_relativelyRepresentable _) (presentationGroupoid_isPullback _)

/-- The transition morphism of `(φ^*ℱ, can)` is the canonical descent datum. -/
theorem objectsFunctor_obj_alpha
    (N : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property) :
    ((objectsFunctor G).obj N).alpha =
      spaceBaseDescent B S hS (objectsGroupoid G) (objectsAtlas G) (objectsAtlas_comm G) N.obj :=
  spaceBaseObj_alpha B S hS _ _ _ N

/-- The transition morphism of `(φ^*ℱ, can)` is the canonical descent datum, written out. -/
theorem objectsFunctor_obj_alpha_heq
    (N : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property) :
    HEq ((objectsFunctor G).obj N).alpha
      (modulePullbackUnflatten (objectsAtlas G) (pullbackTransport N.obj (objectsAtlas_comm G))) :=
  heq_of_eq (objectsFunctor_obj_alpha G N)

/-- The cardinal bounding the affine opens of the presenting scheme of the space of objects and of
the chosen atlas of `R_W`. -/
abbrev chartCardinal : Cardinal.{u} :=
  arrowAtlasCardinal (chartArrows G) (objectsPresentation G).U

end Chart

/-! ### Bounded submodules and a separating family -/

namespace QuasicoherentModule

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

variable {A : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-- **Over a small family of modules, the quasi-coherent modules on a groupoid form a set up to
isomorphism.**  The quasi-coherent modules on a groupoid whose underlying module is isomorphic to
a member of a small family of modules on the space of objects have only a set of isomorphism
classes: over a fixed module, the transition morphisms form a set. -/
theorem exists_small_reps (G : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces B S hS A) {I : Type w} [Small.{u} I]
    (W : I → Modules.{u, u} B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property) :
    ∃ (Ind : Type u) (rep : Ind → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G),
      ∀ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (z : I) (_ : Y.F.obj ≅ W z),
        ∃ i : Ind, Nonempty (rep i ≅ Y) := by
  classical
  have : LocallySmall.{u} (Modules.{u, u} B S hS G.arrows.obj G.arrows.property) :=
    locallySmall_modules_smallEtale B S hS _ _
  let Aset : I → Type (u + 1) := fun z =>
    {a : (modulePullback B S hS G.target).obj (W z) ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS G.source).obj (W z) //
      ∃ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (e : Y.F.obj ≅ W z), transportedTransition Y e = a}
  let Ind := Σ z : I, Aset z
  have : Small.{u} Ind := inferInstance
  let rep : Ind → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G := fun i => Classical.choose i.2.2
  refine ⟨Shrink.{u} Ind, fun b => rep ((equivShrink Ind).symm b), fun Y z e => ?_⟩
  let i : Ind := ⟨z, ⟨transportedTransition Y e, Y, e, rfl⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨e₀, h₀⟩ := Classical.choose_spec i.2.2
  exact ⟨equivShrink Ind i, ⟨eqToIso (congrArg rep ((equivShrink Ind).symm_apply_apply i)) ≪≫
    isoOfTransportedTransitionEq e₀ e h₀⟩⟩

variable (G : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces B S hS A) (M : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G)

/-! The module `φ^*ℱ` on the presenting scheme is spelled throughout as the underlying module of
`(objectsFunctor G).obj ℱ`, never as `(modulePullback _ _ _ (objectsAtlas G)).obj ℱ`, and the
lemmas of the calculus above are applied through their forms taking the module, the transition
morphisms and the inclusions through equations.  An equation between morphisms of `𝒪`-modules
which is compared with another one differing only in the spelling of the implicit objects of a
composite is not decidable by the elaborator or the kernel within their budgets, since
`CategoryTheory.CategoryStruct.comp` is then unfolded before the arguments are compared; see the
implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Groupoids/EquivariantQuasicoherentPullback.lean`. -/

/-- The equivalence of Descent, Proposition 03DX, on the presenting scheme. -/
local macro "chartEqv[" G:term "]" : term =>
  `(objectsQuasicoherentEquivalence (T := (objectsPresentation $G).U)
    (U := (objectsGroupoid $G).objects) rfl)

/-- The transition morphism of `(ℱ, α)` read on the chart `R_W`. -/
def chartModuleTransition :
    (modulePullback B S hS (chartTarget G)).obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F.obj ⟶
      (modulePullback B S hS (chartSource G)).obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F.obj :=
  chartTransition (chartTarget_comp_objectsAtlas G) (chartArrowsMap_comp_source G) M.F.obj M.alpha

/-- **A morphism into `φ^*ℱ` determines a local section**: any two morphisms out of `φ^*ℱ`
agreeing after it agree on the section. -/
def ChartSeparates {EW : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
      (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property}
    (ιW : EW.obj ⟶ ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F.obj)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Opens)
    (x : Γ((((chartEqv[G]).inverse.obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules), O)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (N : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
      (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property) (a b : ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F ⟶ N),
    ιW ≫ a.hom = ιW ≫ b.hom →
      Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U)
          ((chartEqv[G]).inverse.map a).hom O x =
        Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U)
          ((chartEqv[G]).inverse.map b).hom O x

/-- **The closure step on the chart**: every local section of `φ^*ℱ` lies in a bounded
quasi-coherent submodule invariant under the transition morphism read on the chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_eq`, the closure step of
Stacks 077U). -/
theorem exists_chart_closure (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Opens)
    (x : Γ((((chartEqv[G]).inverse.obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules), O)) :
    ∃ (Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules)
      (_ : Z.IsQuasicoherent)
      (EW : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
        (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property)
      (ιW : EW.obj ⟶ ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F.obj)
      (βW : (modulePullback B S hS (chartTarget G)).obj EW.obj ⟶
        (modulePullback B S hS (chartSource G)).obj EW.obj),
      CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z (chartCardinal G) ∧
      Nonempty (EW.obj ≅ (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor (T := (objectsPresentation G).U)
        (U := (objectsGroupoid G).objects) rfl).obj Z) ∧
      Mono ιW ∧ IsTransitionSquare (chartTarget G) (chartSource G) ιW βW
        (chartModuleTransition G M) ∧ ChartSeparates G M ιW O x :=
  exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_eq (T := (objectsPresentation G).U)
    (U := (objectsGroupoid G).objects) rfl (chartSource G) (chartTarget G)
    (chartSource_isFlat G hs) ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F (chartModuleTransition G M) O x

variable {G M}

/-- **A submodule invariant under a transition morphism**: `β` is compatible with the transition
morphism of `Y` along `ι`. -/
abbrev IsInvariantTransition {A' : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    {G' : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces B S hS A'} (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G')
    {E : Modules.{u, u} B S hS G'.objects.obj G'.objects.property} (ι : E ⟶ Y.F.obj)
    (β : (modulePullback B S hS G'.target).obj E ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS G'.source).obj E) :
    Prop :=
  IsTransitionSquare G'.target G'.source ι β Y.alpha

section ChartSubmodule

variable {EW : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
    (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property}
  (ιW : EW.obj ⟶ ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F.obj) (hιW : Mono ιW)
  (βW : (modulePullback B S hS (chartTarget G)).obj EW.obj ⟶
    (modulePullback B S hS (chartSource G)).obj EW.obj)
  (hβW : IsTransitionSquare (chartTarget G) (chartSource G) ιW βW (chartModuleTransition G M))

include hβW in
/-- A submodule of `φ^*ℱ` invariant under the transition morphism read on the chart is invariant
under the transition morphism of `(φ^*ℱ, can)`, the canonical descent datum. -/
theorem exists_chartSubmoduleTransition :
    ∃ β₀ : (modulePullback B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).target).obj EW.obj ⟶
        (modulePullback B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).source).obj EW.obj,
      IsInvariantTransition ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F) ιW β₀ :=
  exists_descentTransition_of_chartTransition'
    (chartTarget_comp_objectsAtlas G) (chartArrowsMap_comp_source G) (chartUnitArrow G)
    (chartUnitArrow_chartTarget G) (chartUnitArrow_chartSource G) (objectsAtlas_comm G)
    (chartUnitArrow_chartArrowsMap G) (Category.assoc _ _ _) M.F.obj M.alpha
    ((GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow_comp_target G).trans
      (GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow_comp_source G).symm) M.unit rfl HEq.rfl
    (objectsFunctor_obj_alpha_heq G M.F) ιW βW hβW

include hιW in
theorem mono_comp_source_chartSubmodule :
    Mono ((modulePullback B S hS ((objectsGroupoid G).comp ≫ (objectsGroupoid G).source)).map
      ιW) :=
  mono_modulePullback_map_of_isFlat ((objectsGroupoid G).comp ≫ (objectsGroupoid G).source)
    (isFlat_comp_comp_source (objectsGroupoid G)
      (isFlat_of_isEtale B S hS (presentationGroupoid_source_isEtale (objectsPresentation G))))
    ιW hιW

include hιW in
theorem mono_identity_source_chartSubmodule :
    Mono ((modulePullback B S hS (GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow (objectsGroupoid G) ≫
      (objectsGroupoid G).source)).map ιW) :=
  mono_modulePullback_map_of_isFlat
    (GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow (objectsGroupoid G) ≫ (objectsGroupoid G).source)
    (isFlat_identityArrow_comp_source (objectsGroupoid G)) ιW hιW

/-- **The submodule of `(φ^*ℱ, can)` cut out by a submodule of `φ^*ℱ` invariant under the
transition morphism read on the chart.** -/
def chartSubmodule : QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G) :=
  restrictedQuasicoherentModule ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F) EW ιW
    (exists_chartSubmoduleTransition ιW βW hβW).choose
    (exists_chartSubmoduleTransition ιW βW hβW).choose_spec
    (mono_comp_source_chartSubmodule ιW hιW) (mono_identity_source_chartSubmodule ιW hιW)

/-- The inclusion of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.chartSubmodule` into
`(φ^*ℱ, can)`. -/
def chartSubmoduleHom : chartSubmodule ιW hιW βW hβW ⟶ (objectsFunctor G).obj M.F :=
  restrictedQuasicoherentModuleHom ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F) EW ιW
    (exists_chartSubmoduleTransition ιW βW hβW).choose
    (exists_chartSubmoduleTransition ιW βW hβW).choose_spec
    (mono_comp_source_chartSubmodule ιW hιW) (mono_identity_source_chartSubmodule ιW hιW)

theorem chartSubmodule_F_obj : (chartSubmodule ιW hιW βW hβW).F.obj = EW.obj := rfl

theorem chartSubmoduleHom_hom_heq : HEq (chartSubmoduleHom ιW hιW βW hβW).hom ιW := HEq.rfl

theorem mono_chartSubmoduleHom_hom : Mono (chartSubmoduleHom ιW hιW βW hβW).hom := hιW

end ChartSubmodule

/-- **A submodule of `(φ^*ℱ, can)` descends to a quasi-coherent submodule of `ℱ`**, by the
equivalence of Stacks 03M3 for the chosen presentation of the space of objects. -/
theorem exists_descent_of_chartModule {Y' : QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G)}
    (j : Y' ⟶ (objectsFunctor G).obj M.F) (hj : Mono j.hom) :
    ∃ (E : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property) (ι : E ⟶ M.F)
      (θ : ((objectsFunctor G).obj E).F.obj ≅ Y'.F.obj),
      Mono ((objectsFunctor G).map ι).hom ∧ ((objectsFunctor G).map ι).hom = θ.hom ≫ j.hom ∧
        E = (objectsFunctor G).objPreimage Y' := by
  let Φ := objectsFunctor G
  let c : Φ.obj (Φ.objPreimage Y') ≅ Y' := Φ.objObjPreimageIso Y'
  let θ : (Φ.obj (Φ.objPreimage Y')).F.obj ≅ Y'.F.obj := (QuasicoherentModule.forget _).mapIso c
  have hι : (Φ.map (Φ.preimage (c.hom ≫ j))).hom = θ.hom ≫ j.hom :=
    congrArg QuasicoherentModule.Hom.hom (Φ.map_preimage _)
  refine ⟨Φ.objPreimage Y', Φ.preimage (c.hom ≫ j), θ, ?_, hι, rfl⟩
  have hθ : Mono θ.hom := ⟨fun g h hgh => by
    simpa only [Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id] using
      congrArg (· ≫ θ.inv) hgh⟩
  have h1 : Mono (θ.hom ≫ j.hom) := @mono_comp _ _ _ _ _ θ.hom hθ j.hom hj
  rw [hι]
  exact h1

/-- **A submodule of `ℱ` whose inverse image along the atlas is invariant under the transition
morphism read on the chart is invariant under `α`.** -/
theorem exists_transition_of_chart (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom)
    {E : Modules.{u, u} B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property} (ι : E ⟶ M.F.obj) (hι : Mono ι)
    {N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
      (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property}
    (hN : N = (modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).obj M.F.obj)
    {P : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
      (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property}
    (hP : P = (modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).obj E)
    (f : P ⟶ N) (hf : HEq f ((modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).map ι))
    {αW : (modulePullback B S hS (chartTarget G)).obj N ⟶
      (modulePullback B S hS (chartSource G)).obj N}
    (hαW : HEq αW (chartTransition (chartTarget_comp_objectsAtlas G)
      (chartArrowsMap_comp_source G) M.F.obj M.alpha))
    {EW EW' : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
      (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property}
    (ιW : EW ⟶ N)
    (βW : (modulePullback B S hS (chartTarget G)).obj EW ⟶
      (modulePullback B S hS (chartSource G)).obj EW)
    (hβW : IsTransitionSquare (chartTarget G) (chartSource G) ιW βW αW)
    (ιW' : EW' ⟶ N) (hEW : EW' = EW) (hιW' : HEq ιW' ιW)
    (θ : P ≅ EW') (hθ : f = θ.hom ≫ ιW') :
    ∃ β : (modulePullback B S hS G.target).obj E ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS G.source).obj E,
      IsInvariantTransition M ι β := by
  subst hN hP hEW
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hιW'
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hf
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hαW
  have : (modulePullback B S hS (chartArrowsMap G)).Faithful :=
    faithful_modulePullback_chartArrowsMap G
  have : Mono ((modulePullback B S hS G.source).map ι) :=
    mono_modulePullback_map_of_isFlat _ hs _ hι
  have hζ : ((modulePullback B S hS (chartTarget G)).map θ.hom ≫ βW ≫
      (modulePullback B S hS (chartSource G)).map θ.inv) ≫
        (modulePullback B S hS (chartSource G)).map
          ((modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).map ι) =
      (modulePullback B S hS (chartTarget G)).map
          ((modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).map ι) ≫
        chartTransition (chartTarget_comp_objectsAtlas G) (chartArrowsMap_comp_source G) M.F.obj
          M.alpha := by
    unfold IsTransitionSquare at hβW
    rw [hθ, Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc, Category.assoc,
      Iso.map_inv_hom_id_assoc, hβW, Category.assoc]
  exact exists_comp_eq_of_chart (chartTarget_comp_objectsAtlas G) (chartArrowsMap_comp_source G)
    ι M.alpha _ ((modulePullbackFlatten_naturality (objectsAtlas G) ι _ _ hζ).trans
      (congrArg (_ ≫ ·) (modulePullbackFlatten_chartTransition _ _ M.F.obj M.alpha)))

/-- A morphism of quasi-coherent modules on the groupoid, read on the chart. -/
def chartHom {N : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G} (a : M ⟶ N) :
    ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F ⟶ ((objectsFunctor G).obj N.F).F :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk ((objectsFunctor G).map (ObjectProperty.homMk a.hom)).hom

theorem chartHom_hom {N : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G} (a : M ⟶ N) :
    (chartHom a).hom = ((objectsFunctor G).map (ObjectProperty.homMk a.hom)).hom := rfl

variable (G) in
/-- Two morphisms out of a quasi-coherent module on the groupoid agree, read on the chart, on a
local section. -/
def ChartAgree {N : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G} (a b : M ⟶ N)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Opens)
    (x : Γ((((chartEqv[G]).inverse.obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules), O)) : Prop :=
  Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U)
      ((chartEqv[G]).inverse.map (chartHom a)).hom O x =
    Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U)
      ((chartEqv[G]).inverse.map (chartHom b)).hom O x

variable (G) in
/-- **A morphism into `(ℱ, α)` determines a local section on the chart**: any two morphisms out
of `(ℱ, α)` agreeing after it agree, read on the chart, on the section. -/
def GroupoidSeparates {M' : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G} (j : M' ⟶ M)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Opens)
    (x : Γ((((chartEqv[G]).inverse.obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules), O)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (N : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (a b : M ⟶ N), j ≫ a = j ≫ b → ChartAgree G a b O x

/-- A morphism `j : M' ⟶ M` whose image under `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.objectsFunctor` factors as
an isomorphism followed by a morphism determining a local section determines that section. -/
theorem groupoidSeparates_of_chartSeparates {M' : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G} (j : M' ⟶ M)
    {EW : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
      (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property}
    {ιW : EW.obj ⟶ ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F.obj}
    {O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Opens}
    {x : Γ((((chartEqv[G]).inverse.obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules), O)}
    (hdet : ChartSeparates G M ιW O x)
    {EW' : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (objectsGroupoid G).objects.obj
      (objectsGroupoid G).objects.property}
    (ιW' : EW' ⟶ ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F.obj) (hEW : EW' = EW.obj) (hιW' : HEq ιW' ιW)
    (θ : ((objectsFunctor G).obj M'.F).F.obj ≅ EW')
    (hθ : ((objectsFunctor G).map (ObjectProperty.homMk j.hom)).hom = θ.hom ≫ ιW') :
    GroupoidSeparates G j O x := by
  subst hEW
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hιW'
  intro N a b hab
  unfold ChartAgree
  apply hdet ((objectsFunctor G).obj N.F).F (chartHom a) (chartHom b)
  have h1 : (ObjectProperty.homMk j.hom : M'.F ⟶ M.F) ≫ ObjectProperty.homMk a.hom =
      ObjectProperty.homMk j.hom ≫ ObjectProperty.homMk b.hom :=
    ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (congrArg QuasicoherentModule.Hom.hom hab)
  have h3 := congrArg (fun k => ((objectsFunctor G).map k).hom) h1
  simp only [Functor.map_comp, QuasicoherentModule.comp_hom, hθ, Category.assoc] at h3
  rw [chartHom_hom, chartHom_hom]
  exact (Iso.cancel_iso_hom_left θ _ _).1 h3

variable (G)

/-- **Every local section on the chart of a quasi-coherent module on a flat groupoid lies in a
bounded submodule.**  Let `(ℱ, α)` be a quasi-coherent module on a groupoid with flat source,
and `x` a local section of the Zariski module on the presenting scheme `W` of the space of objects
corresponding to `φ^*ℱ`.  There is a submodule `j : (ℰ, β) ⟶ (ℱ, α)` such that `ℰ` is the
descent of a quasi-coherent module `Y'` on the groupoid of the presentation whose underlying
module is the associated module of a `κ`-generated quasi-coherent Zariski module on `W`, and any
two morphisms out of `(ℱ, α)` which agree after `j` agree on `x`. -/
theorem exists_bounded_submodule_of_chart_section (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom)
    (M : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Opens)
    (x : Γ((((chartEqv[G]).inverse.obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules), O)) :
    ∃ (M' : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (j : M' ⟶ M)
      (Y' : QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G))
      (_ : M'.F = (objectsFunctor G).objPreimage Y')
      (Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules)
      (_ : Z.IsQuasicoherent),
      CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z (chartCardinal G) ∧
      Nonempty (Y'.F.obj ≅ (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor (T := (objectsPresentation G).U)
        (U := (objectsGroupoid G).objects) rfl).obj Z) ∧
      GroupoidSeparates G j O x := by
  obtain ⟨Z, hZ, EW, ιW, βW, hZκ, ⟨eEW⟩, hιW, hβW, hdetW⟩ := exists_chart_closure G M hs O x
  obtain ⟨E, ι, θ, hι, hφι, hE⟩ := exists_descent_of_chartModule
    (chartSubmoduleHom ιW hιW βW hβW) (mono_chartSubmoduleHom_hom ιW hιW βW hβW)
  have hιU : Mono ι.hom := by
    have : (modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).Faithful :=
      faithful_modulePullback_objectsAtlas G
    exact (modulePullback B S hS (objectsAtlas G)).mono_of_mono_map hι
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := exists_transition_of_chart hs ι.hom hιU rfl rfl _ HEq.rfl HEq.rfl ιW βW hβW
    _ (chartSubmodule_F_obj ιW hιW βW hβW) (chartSubmoduleHom_hom_heq ιW hιW βW hβW) θ hφι
  have hc := mono_modulePullback_map_of_isFlat (G.comp ≫ G.source)
    (isFlat_comp_comp_source G hs) _ hιU
  have he := mono_modulePullback_map_of_isFlat
    (GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.identityArrow G ≫ G.source)
    (isFlat_identityArrow_comp_source G) _ hιU
  refine ⟨restrictedQuasicoherentModule M E ι.hom β hβ hc he,
    restrictedQuasicoherentModuleHom M E ι.hom β hβ hc he, chartSubmodule ιW hιW βW hβW, hE, Z,
    hZ, hZκ, ⟨eqToIso (chartSubmodule_F_obj ιW hιW βW hβW) ≪≫ eEW⟩, ?_⟩
  exact groupoidSeparates_of_chartSeparates _ hdetW _ (chartSubmodule_F_obj ιW hιW βW hβW)
    (chartSubmoduleHom_hom_heq ιW hιW βW hβW) θ hφι

/-- Two morphisms out of a quasi-coherent module on a flat groupoid agree, read on the chart, on
every local section as soon as they agree after every morphism from a member of a family
containing, up to isomorphism, the bounded submodules of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_bounded_submodule_of_chart_section`. -/
theorem app_eq_of_separating_bounded (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom)
    {Q : ObjectProperty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules}
    (hPQ : ∀ Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules,
      Z.IsQuasicoherent → CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z (chartCardinal G) →
        Q.isoClosure Z)
    {Ind₀ : Type u} {rep₀ : Ind₀ → QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G)}
    (hrep₀ : ∀ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G)) (z : Subtype Q)
      (_ : Y.F.obj ≅ (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor (T := (objectsPresentation G).U)
        (U := (objectsGroupoid G).objects) rfl).obj z.1),
        ∃ i : Ind₀, Nonempty (rep₀ i ≅ Y))
    {Ind : Type u} {rep : Ind → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G}
    (hrep : ∀ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (i₀ : Ind₀)
      (_ : Y.F.obj ≅ ((objectsFunctor G).objPreimage (rep₀ i₀)).obj),
        ∃ i : Ind, Nonempty (rep i ≅ Y))
    {M M' : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G} {a b : M ⟶ M'}
    (hab : ∀ (X : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G), ObjectProperty.ofObj rep X →
      ∀ h : X ⟶ M, h ≫ a = h ≫ b)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Opens)
    (x : Γ((((chartEqv[G]).inverse.obj ((objectsFunctor G).obj M.F).F).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules), O)) :
    ChartAgree G a b O x := by
  obtain ⟨M'', j, Y', hY', Z, hZ, hZκ, ⟨eY⟩, hdet⟩ :=
    exists_bounded_submodule_of_chart_section G hs M O x
  obtain ⟨Z₀, hZ₀, ⟨eZ⟩⟩ := hPQ Z hZ hZκ
  obtain ⟨i₀, ⟨e₀⟩⟩ := hrep₀ Y' ⟨Z₀, hZ₀⟩ (eY ≪≫
    (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor (T := (objectsPresentation G).U)
      (U := (objectsGroupoid G).objects) rfl).mapIso eZ)
  have eF : M''.F.obj ≅ ((objectsFunctor G).objPreimage (rep₀ i₀)).obj := by
    rw [hY']
    exact (ObjectProperty.ι _).mapIso ((objectsFunctor G).preimageIso
      ((objectsFunctor G).objObjPreimageIso Y' ≪≫ e₀.symm ≪≫
        ((objectsFunctor G).objObjPreimageIso (rep₀ i₀)).symm))
  obtain ⟨i, ⟨ei⟩⟩ := hrep M'' i₀ eF
  have h := hab (rep i) (ObjectProperty.ofObj_apply rep i) (ei.hom ≫ j)
  have h' : j ≫ a = j ≫ b := by
    rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc] at h
    exact (Iso.cancel_iso_hom_left ei _ _).1 h
  exact hdet M' a b h'

/-- Two morphisms out of a quasi-coherent module on a flat groupoid are equal as soon as they
agree after every morphism from a member of a family containing, up to isomorphism, the bounded
submodules of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_bounded_submodule_of_chart_section`. -/
theorem eq_of_separating_bounded (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom)
    {Q : ObjectProperty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules}
    (hPQ : ∀ Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (objectsPresentation G).U).Modules,
      Z.IsQuasicoherent → CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z (chartCardinal G) →
        Q.isoClosure Z)
    {Ind₀ : Type u} {rep₀ : Ind₀ → QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G)}
    (hrep₀ : ∀ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS (objectsGroupoid G)) (z : Subtype Q)
      (_ : Y.F.obj ≅ (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor (T := (objectsPresentation G).U)
        (U := (objectsGroupoid G).objects) rfl).obj z.1),
        ∃ i : Ind₀, Nonempty (rep₀ i ≅ Y))
    {Ind : Type u} {rep : Ind → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G}
    (hrep : ∀ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (i₀ : Ind₀)
      (_ : Y.F.obj ≅ ((objectsFunctor G).objPreimage (rep₀ i₀)).obj),
        ∃ i : Ind, Nonempty (rep i ≅ Y))
    {M M' : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G} {a b : M ⟶ M'}
    (hab : ∀ (X : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G), ObjectProperty.ofObj rep X →
      ∀ h : X ⟶ M, h ≫ a = h ≫ b) : a = b := by
  have hq : (chartEqv[G]).inverse.map (chartHom a) = (chartEqv[G]).inverse.map (chartHom b) :=
    ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (scheme_modules_hom_ext_of_app_apply _ _
      (app_eq_of_separating_bounded G hs hPQ hrep₀ hrep hab))
  have h1 := congrArg (fun k => k.hom) ((chartEqv[G]).inverse.map_injective hq)
  rw [chartHom_hom, chartHom_hom] at h1
  have h2 := (objectsFunctor G).map_injective (QuasicoherentModule.Hom.ext h1)
  exact QuasicoherentModule.Hom.ext (congrArg (fun k => k.hom) h2)

/-- **A separating family of quasi-coherent modules on a groupoid in algebraic spaces with flat
source**, indexed by a type of the universe of the schemes.  The bounded submodules of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_bounded_submodule_of_chart_section` have
a set of isomorphism classes, and a set of representatives separates. -/
theorem exists_isSeparating (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom) :
    ∃ (β : Type u) (f : β → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G),
      (ObjectProperty.ofObj f).IsSeparating := by
  classical
  let P := objectsPresentation G
  let Pz : ObjectProperty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj P.U).Modules := fun M =>
    M.IsQuasicoherent ∧ CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated M (chartCardinal G)
  have : ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.{u}
      (fun M : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj P.U).Modules =>
        CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated M (chartCardinal G)) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGenerated.essentiallySmall_isCardinalGenerated
      (X := ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj P.U).toRingedSpace) (chartCardinal G)
  have : ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.{u} Pz :=
    ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.of_le fun _ h => h.2
  obtain ⟨Q, hQsmall, -, hPQ⟩ := ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.exists_small_le.{u} Pz
  have := hQsmall
  obtain ⟨Ind₀, rep₀, hrep₀⟩ := exists_small_reps (objectsGroupoid G)
    (fun z : Subtype Q => (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor (T := P.U)
      (U := (objectsGroupoid G).objects) rfl).obj z.1)
  obtain ⟨Ind, rep, hrep⟩ := exists_small_reps G
    (fun i : Ind₀ => ((objectsFunctor G).objPreimage (rep₀ i)).obj)
  exact ⟨Ind, rep, fun M M' a b hab =>
    eq_of_separating_bounded G hs (fun Z hZ hZκ => hPQ Z ⟨hZ, hZκ⟩) hrep₀ hrep hab⟩

/-- **`QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)` has a separator** when the source is flat. -/
theorem hasSeparator (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom) :
    HasSeparator (QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) := by
  obtain ⟨β, f, hf⟩ := exists_isSeparating G hs
  exact ⟨∐ f, (isSeparator_sigma f).2 hf⟩

/-- **The quasi-coherent modules on a groupoid in algebraic spaces with flat source and target
form a Grothendieck abelian category.** -/
theorem isGrothendieckAbelian (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom)
    (ht : IsFlat B S hS G.target.hom) :
    letI := abelian_of_closure G hs ht
    IsGrothendieckAbelian.{u} (QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) :=
  let := abelian_of_closure G hs ht
  have := hasSeparator G hs
  isGrothendieckAbelian_of_hasSeparator G hs ht

/-- **Stacks 0780.**  Let `(U, R, s, t, c)` be a groupoid in algebraic spaces with `s` and `t`
flat.  There is a family `F : T → QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)` indexed by a type `T` of the universe of
the schemes, that is by a set, such that every quasi-coherent module on the groupoid is the
directed colimit of those of its submodules which are isomorphic to a member of the family: the
subobjects isomorphic to a member of the family form a filtered category, and the cocone of their
inclusions is a colimit cocone. -/
@[stacks 0780 "The index type `T` lives in the universe `u` of the schemes of the site, so the \
family is a set.  The proof goes through a separating family of bounded submodules, built on an \
étale chart of the arrows over a presentation of the space of objects, and the Grothendieck \
property of `QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)`."]
theorem exists_small_generating_family (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom)
    (ht : IsFlat B S hS G.target.hom) :
    ∃ (T : Type u) (F : T → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G),
      ∀ M : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G,
        IsFiltered (IsomorphicGeneratorSubobject T F M) ∧
          Nonempty (IsColimit (isomorphicGeneratorSubobjectCocone T F M)) := by
  let := abelian_of_closure G hs ht
  have := isGrothendieckAbelian G hs ht
  obtain ⟨T, F, hF⟩ := IsGrothendieckAbelian.exists_family_isFiltered_isColimit.{u}
    (C := QuasicoherentModule B S hS G)
  exact ⟨T, F, hF⟩

end QuasicoherentModule

